From 46941917680d27ab63f9607d8b9171d6a16b4114 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cruz <cruz@tbu.net>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 19:57:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 120/206] docs(shorebird): record the sweep for other
 blob-as-Image uses

Task 75 fixed two tests that were reading a zero-length JIT instructions
blob as an Image. This records the sweep for anything else of that shape,
and the verdict on bin_to_assembly.py's `.balign 32`.

runtime/ constructs an Image in 22 places outside the class's own
definition. Three are ours; the other nineteen are upstream's and every
one of them sits either inside `#if defined(DART_PRECOMPILED_RUNTIME)` or
behind Snapshot::IncludesCode(), which a core snapshot fails. So none of
them can be reached with one of these blobs, and the two tests already
fixed were the only two. The three tests that still reach into dart::bin
take vm_snapshot_data, not the instructions blob: that one is real, 13646
bytes, and is read through Snapshot::SetupFromBuffer, which checks a
magic number and a version string first.

`.balign 32` stays as it is. bin_to_assembly.py is upstream-pristine,
every symbol it emits here comes from --snapshot_kind=core, and both
instructions blobs of a core snapshot are 0 bytes in all three
configurations we build. Upstream never parses them, and where a
linked-in blob really can reach a reader it checks rather than trusts the
assembler -- ImageReader::VerifyAlignment turns a misaligned image into
an ApiError. Raising the directive to 64 would buy nothing and would put
us off upstream for no reason.

What catches this class of mistake is the ASSERT in Image's constructor,
and only a build that compiles ASSERT in can catch it: measured,
_kDartVmSnapshotInstructions is 0 mod 64 in the Release build and 32 mod
64 in the Debug simulator one. That is why sim_only_tests_check.sh runs
the full set in the second.

Negative control for that last claim: misaligning FakeInstructionsImage
by 32 fails exactly Shorebird_BaseInstructionRangeSpansTheImage and
Shorebird_PcQueriesAnswerForTheRightImage in the Debug simulator build,
while Release still reports 151 of 151.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/runtime/vm/shorebird/shorebird_test.cc b/runtime/vm/shorebird/shorebird_test.cc
index 591e050b5cf..eadb2922093 100644
--- a/runtime/vm/shorebird/shorebird_test.cc
+++ b/runtime/vm/shorebird/shorebird_test.cc
@@ -55,6 +55,36 @@ static std::vector<uint8_t> MakeHeader(
 // what finally made the ASSERT at image_snapshot.h:47 fire and exposed all of
 // the above.
 //
+// Swept the tree for anything else of the same shape. runtime/ constructs an
+// Image in 22 places outside the class's own definition. Three are ours:
+// shorebird.cc:173 (BaseSnapshotInstructionsEnd), shorebird.cc:190 (PcInImage)
+// and analyze_snapshot_api_impl.cc:1769 (InstructionsRegionSize). The other
+// nineteen are upstream's, and every one of them sits either inside
+// `#if defined(DART_PRECOMPILED_RUNTIME)` or behind Snapshot::IncludesCode(),
+// which a core snapshot fails -- so none of them can be reached with one of
+// these blobs. The two tests below were the only two, and they are fixed.
+//
+// The three tests that still reach into dart::bin do not repeat it: they take
+// vm_snapshot_data, not the instructions blob. That one is real -- 13646 bytes
+// -- and is read through Snapshot::SetupFromBuffer, which checks a magic number
+// and a version string before anything is believed. A different contract, and
+// not one that can silently succeed on a random function.
+//
+// So `.balign 32` is a constraint to remember, not a bug to fix.
+// bin_to_assembly.py is upstream-pristine, every symbol it emits here comes
+// from --snapshot_kind=core, and both instructions blobs of a core snapshot are
+// 0 bytes in all three of our configurations. Upstream never parses them; where
+// a linked-in blob really can reach a reader, it checks rather than trusts the
+// assembler -- ImageReader::VerifyAlignment (image_snapshot.cc:2165) turns a
+// misaligned image into an ApiError. Raising the directive to 64 would buy
+// nothing and would put us off upstream for no reason.
+//
+// What catches this class of mistake is the ASSERT at image_snapshot.h:47, and
+// it only catches it in a build that compiles ASSERT in. That is the whole
+// reason sim_only_tests_check.sh runs the full set in the Debug simulator
+// build: measured, _kDartVmSnapshotInstructions is 0 mod 64 in ReleaseARM64 and
+// 32 mod 64 in DebugSIMARM64, so Release alone would never have said a word.
+//
 // So: build one. The header is two words -- total size, then 0 for "no
 // InstructionsSection", which is what makes ExtraInfo() return nullptr --
 // followed by payload starting at Image::kHeaderSize == kObjectStartAlignment.
-- 
